Meh, this was a hard, hard game. I decided I'd try to go atheist as well
as wish/genoless, and it sure changed a lot of the earlygame dynamics. No
easy BUC-id meant that I had to rely heavily on pets, and lack of holy
water made it very, very hard to get things identified.

I found a single bonesfile, with a poor wizard who left behind a magic
lamp, a cloak of MR, as well as some unholy water.

After a while I identified remove curse, which meant it was time to make
some holy water - but the first 2 scrolls gave me nothing but uncursed
water, how fun. 

It took ages to muddle through the early and midgame, no bag of holding,
and shitty AC meant every fight was hard, and I had to pay constant
attention to my hitpoints.

Once I finally got holy water, I blessed 5 scrolls of identify, NEITHER
gave me full id, offcourse.

The only thing the RNG was generous with was magic markers, 4 of them
plus the PYEC would mean lots of scrolls later on.

I finally found enchant armor, and then stupidly lost any knowledge
about it thanks to engraving a empty wand of fire vs a mind
flayer. Clever stuff, I didn't find it again until very late in the
game, thus the horrible AC vs demogorgon mentioned above.

The RNG had some sense of humour though, since I managed to FIND 2 wands
of wishing, both at 0:2, aswell as another magic lamp. With the castle
wand at 0:3, that's a sick amount of wishes, not that I planned on using
any, offcourse.

I very slowly managed to work my way all the way down to the vibrating
square, and slowly mucking about finally gave me a bag of holding,
scrolls of enchant armor, and some dragon scale mail - not silver or
gray offcourse :)

Enchanting weapons and armor was fun too - I got ONE SINGLE ARMOR PIECE
at +5, weapons where at +6 all the time, even after reenchanting after hitting
disenchanters, armor where at +4, and my elven helmet stayed at +6. Not
that it mattered much, dual +6 silver sabres along with a +6 ring of
increase damage (thanks PYEC) made me do sick amounts of damage. I
wouldn't dare think how much grayswandir would have added.

I was fully intent on going through to astral with -12 AC if I hadn't
found any scrolls of enchant armor, thus the heavy alchemy, but luckily
I didn't have to try :o

My stupidest mistake ever was losing polypile: I had tamed a new pet,
and zapped some poly at it trying to get a good one - polymorphing the
corpses it was standing on in the process :(

I broke polypile to make 2 candy bars, how delightful. Never polypiled
anything else, however, so it still sort of stands, I guess.

The most fun fight was probably the one vs 2 arch liches, demogorgon and
yeenoghu, all with -11 AC and burdened. I was trying to bait a arch-lich
away from the upstairs, but he decided to summon a friend instead, and
soon one of them had old demo gating in, and yeenoghu followed shortly
after. It was touch and go for a while, but wands of fire made me able
to slowly get to the upstairs, without getting killed by demogorgon in
the process.


Offcourse they all ran to the upstairs and escaped, leading to 

http://rasmus.uib.no/~st12305/sa/fucked.gif :)

I used a ring of poly control along with some scrolls of teleportation
while confused to level port back to my stash, got unburdened and
returned to the level above, where some nice chickatrices decided to
spawn :)


Pretty statues! Second time I've seen demogorgon, the first time a
helpful orcus summoned him for my extinctionist wizard.

I spent a looong time getting prepared for the endgame, and perhaps I
was overly cautious - but this was the first in a dousin of tourists to make it
this far, and I didn't want to take any chances.


The PYEC definately is a amazing artifact, making wands extremely
powerful - I'd definately try a tourist if I'd ever go atheist illiterate.

The lategame was easy, thanks to plenty of wands of death, finally
levitation, and -30 AC, as well as plenty of health.

The riders never got close, except for death, and he only got some
hitpoints twice - he died in 2 hits :D

God I love this game.


